sequenceDiagram
    autonumber

    actor Visitor
    participant Browser
    participant BFF as BFF / API
    participant Context as Return context mechanism
    participant IdP as Identity Provider
    participant Identity as Identity adapter
    participant Ratings as Ratings module
    participant Catalogue as Catalogue contract
    participant DB as PostgreSQL
    participant Telemetry

    Visitor->>Browser: Select a valid rating value and confirm
    Browser->>BFF: Confirm rating intent (gameId, ratingValue)
    BFF->>BFF: Validate the input before authentication
    BFF->>Context: Store or encode short-lived, tamper-resistant context
    Context-->>BFF: Opaque state, nonce and expiry
    BFF-->>Browser: Redirect to the established identity flow
    Browser->>IdP: Authenticate using Authorization Code with PKCE
    IdP-->>Browser: Return authorization result
    Browser->>BFF: Authentication callback with opaque state
    BFF->>Identity: Resolve validated issuer and subject
    Identity-->>BFF: Stable UserId
    BFF->>Context: Validate and atomically consume return context

    alt Context invalid, expired or replayed
        Context-->>BFF: Reject consumption
        BFF-->>Browser: Return a safe view or trusted current state
        Note over BFF,Ratings: Do not execute the rating command
    else First valid consumption
        Context-->>BFF: gameId, ratingValue and approved return destination
        BFF->>Ratings: Create personal rating exactly once
        Ratings->>Catalogue: Request current rating eligibility evidence
        Catalogue-->>Ratings: Supported game, release evidence and decision

        alt Game is not eligible
            Ratings-->>BFF: RATING_NOT_ELIGIBLE with stable reason
            BFF->>Telemetry: Record safe rejection telemetry
            BFF-->>Browser: Resume the same game with disabled rating state
        else Game is eligible
            Ratings->>DB: Atomically enforce uniqueness, create rating and update aggregate statistics
            DB-->>Ratings: Personal rating and current aggregate context
            Ratings->>Telemetry: Record success without sensitive data
            Ratings-->>BFF: Personal and aggregate results as separate fields
            BFF-->>Browser: Resume the same game context
            Browser-->>Visitor: Show saved personal rating and updated aggregate
        end
    end

    Note over Visitor,Telemetry: Client data never supplies the trusted rating owner
